{"id":"b72c632f5deae9c3","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-ax-rep.md","title":"Axiom Schema of Replacement","display":"ax-rep — Axiom Schema of Replacement","type":"axiom","metadata":{"type":"axiom","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-ax-rep","aliases":["58-ax-rep"],"display":"ax-rep — Axiom Schema of Replacement","depends_on":["[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-free-variable]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"axiom"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-ax-rep"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-ax-rep</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"ax-rep — Axiom Schema of Replacement"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_{\\in}\">\\(\\Sigma_{\\in}\\)</span> is the first-order signature of set theory, with no nonlogical function or constant symbols and with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\in\">\\(\\in\\)</span> as its sole binary relation symbol (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\">\\(\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a,b,x,y,p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\">\\(a,b,x,y,p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\)</span> are pairwise distinct and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\Sigma_{\\in}}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{x,y,p_i:i\\in n\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{FV}_{\\Sigma_{\\in}}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{x,y,p_i:i\\in n\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\">\\(\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\)</span> denotes this fixed formula with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec p=\\langle p_i:i\\in n\\rangle\">\\(\\vec p=\\langle p_i:i\\in n\\rangle\\)</span>; the displayed finite block <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}\">\\(\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}\\)</span> is empty when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=0\">\\(n=0\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}rep}_{\\varphi,n}\\vdash\n\\forall a\\,\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\\forall x\\in a\\;\\exists!y\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr]\n\\to\n\\exists b\\;\\forall y\\;\n\\bigl(y\\in b\\leftrightarrow\\exists x\\in a\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}rep}_{\\varphi,n}\\vdash\n\\forall a\\,\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\\forall x\\in a\\;\\exists!y\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr]\n\\to\n\\exists b\\;\\forall y\\;\n\\bigl(y\\in b\\leftrightarrow\\exists x\\in a\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is a metalevel schema: one object-language sentence is supplied for every finite <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> and every admissible formula <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span>.  Formulas and finite tuples are not quantified over inside the first-order language of set theory.</li>\n<li>The uniqueness premise is functional only on the displayed set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span>; Replacement then collects exactly its image.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-free-variable","status":"resolved","id":"715a32e91161b34f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-free-variable]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Sigma_{\\in}$ is the first-order signature of set theory, with no nonlogical function or constant symbols and with $\\in$ as its sole binary relation symbol (see [[58-df-formula]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-free-variable","status":"resolved","id":"715a32e91161b34f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$a,b,x,y,p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S$ are pairwise distinct and $\\operatorname{FV}_{\\Sigma_{\\in}}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{x,y,p_i:i\\in n\\}$ (see [[58-df-free-variable]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma_{\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"\\in","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma_{\\in})","display":false},{"tex":"a,b,x,y,p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{FV}_{\\Sigma_{\\in}}(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{x,y,p_i:i\\in n\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)","display":false},{"tex":"\\vec p=\\langle p_i:i\\in n\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}","display":false},{"tex":"n=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}rep}_{\\varphi,n}\\vdash\n\\forall a\\,\\forall p_0\\cdots\\forall p_{n-1}\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\bigl[\\forall x\\in a\\;\\exists!y\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr]\n\\to\n\\exists b\\;\\forall y\\;\n\\bigl(y\\in b\\leftrightarrow\\exists x\\in a\\;\\varphi(x,y,\\vec p)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"a","display":false}],"bytes":1506,"backlinks":[{"id":"ada70e665488a6bd","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"da27abf5af2ad534","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"0849bf4363d60a31","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"c9b0bb6a6dbf3b72","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-21","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-ax-rep.md|58-ax-rep]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["65418b505fc53093","715a32e91161b34f"]}